#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133516 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/id #uuid "38b4473a-f956-5af5-863b-387dc10b4924" :question/math-academy-id "e-13362" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n${e^{-x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}x < 0$,\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for\n\n$$\nx \\geq 0\n$$\n\nthe cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\n{0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0, \\\\ \\int_{0}^{x}f(t)dt,\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge 0\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{x}f(t)dt &= \\int_{0}^{x}e^{-t}dt \\\\\n&= \\left.- e^{-t}\\right|_{0}^{x} \\\\\n&=-e^{-x} + 1 \\\\\n&= 1 - e^{-x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\n{0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0, \\\\ 1 - e^{-x},\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge 0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133517 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "98dd834c-ac74-5cdd-88ee-060fd9ac689d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13363" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n$f(x) = e^{-\\mid 2x \\mid}, \\quad x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$,\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\n{\\int_{- ∞}^{x}e^{2t}dt,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0, \\\\ \\int_{- ∞}^{0}e^{2t}dt + \\int_{0}^{x}e^{-2t}dt,\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge 0\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x \\leq 0$, we have\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{- ∞}^{x}e^{2t}dt|= \\left.\\frac{e^{2t}}{2}\\right|_{- ∞}^{x}; = \\frac{e^{2x}}{2}$,\nTherefore,\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{- ∞}^{0}e^{2t}dt|= \\left.\\frac{e^{2x}}{2}\\right|_{x = 0}; = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n- If $x > 0$, we have\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{x}e^{-2t}dt|= \\left.- \\frac{e^{-2t}}{2}\\right|_{0}^{x}; =-\\frac{e^{-2x}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}$.\nAs a result, we get\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{- ∞}^{0}e^{2t}dt + \\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{x}e^{-2t}dt|= \\frac{1}{2} + (-\\frac{e^{-2x}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}); = 1 - \\frac{e^{-2x}}{2}$.\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\n{\\frac{e^{2x}}{2},\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0, \\\\ 1 - \\frac{e^{-2x}}{2},\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge 0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/id #uuid "4159a407-ea9f-5728-b219-bf1afab732a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-13364" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n${\\frac{1}{72}x,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 12, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$,\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\leq 12\n$$\n\nthe cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\n{0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0 \\\\ \\int_{0}^{x}f(t)dt,\\end{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 12; 1, \\mid x > 12\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{x}f(t)dt &= \\int_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{72}tdt \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{1}{144}t^{2}\\right|_{0}^{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{144}x^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\n{0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0 \\\\ \\frac{x^{2}}{144},\\end{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 12; 1, \\mid x > 12\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "707e3b49-9c13-50d8-8a7f-c4d5ec44e0ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-13365" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n${0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 5 \\\\ \\frac{x^{2} - 25}{75},\\end{vmatrix}5 \\le x \\le 10; 1, \\mid x > 10$,\n\nfind $P(2\\leq X \\leq 6)$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(2 \\le X \\le 6) &= P(2 < X \\le 6) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 6) - P(X \\le 2) \\\\\n&= F(6) - F(2) \\\\\n&= \\frac{6^{2} - 25}{75} - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{11}{75}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "8695f467-02b5-5934-9aba-7e6cf9cbc235" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131036}] :question/id #uuid "b6a0e95b-94bf-5003-b9b0-2bdf03b33051" :question/math-academy-id "q-185532" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n$f(x) = {\\frac{2}{21}x,\\begin{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\nits cumulative distribution function is\n$F(x) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 2 \\\\ h(x),\\end{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 5; 1, \\mid x > 5$\nwhere $h(x) =$ {{field-1}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "1a878c16-55d3-55d7-a28d-76c0dd451c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131062}] :question/id #uuid "445cea8c-2aa7-58ac-ac1e-76b49bacb6c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-210758" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n$f(x) = {6e^{-6x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}x < 0$\nits cumulative distribution function is\n$F(x) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0 \\\\ h(x),\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge 0$\nwhere $h(x) =$ {{field-1}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "13407dc0-5b13-5eaa-91b6-bca274b27437" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131063}] :question/id #uuid "1bbb59a5-e080-5eb3-8f00-497d7dc7343f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210766" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n$f(x) = (e^{x})/((1 + e^{x})^{2}), x ∈ (- ∞, ∞)$,\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$.\n\n$F(x) =$\n{{field-1}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7a0ed64-5dc8-5618-ac34-994a571e5fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133267} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c9b1b9-6e2b-5328-8049-3b1b071cdc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133268} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6547f1-96a8-53cf-916f-dc7feeffac31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133269} {:answer/id #uuid "fc294213-b5db-58f4-9a40-7031b00175a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1 + x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133270} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4b0d75-cecb-501a-a659-257ee4c87a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133271}] :answer-field/id #uuid "cf38f8f6-64a3-5a95-aeb0-d81da3820d46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133266}] :question/id #uuid "c465042c-a7c3-596c-abfd-e2cc0c1e779a" :question/math-academy-id "q-89137" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n$f(x) = {\\frac{1}{x^{2}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}x < 1$\nits cumulative distribution function is\n$F(x) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 1 \\\\ h(x),\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge 1$.\nFind the function $h(x)$."}]}
